.TH focusforge-cli-export 1  "export 0.1.0-rc.4" 
.SH NAME
focusforge\-cli\-export \- Turn a project into an image file: the image with `\-o`, the Z\-Map with `\-\-zmap`, either or both in one invocation. At least one of the two is required. This is the only command that writes an image
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfocusforge\-cli export\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-zmap\fR] [\fB\-\-checkpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-tiff\-bits\fR] [\fB\-\-tiff\-compression\fR] [\fB\-\-png\-bits\fR] [\fB\-\-png\-compression\fR] [\fB\-\-jpeg\-quality\fR] [\fB\-\-jpeg\-subsampling\fR] [\fB\-\-exif\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-\-icc\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-xmp\fR] [\fB\-\-iptc\fR] [\fB\-\-frame\fR] [\fB\-\-frame\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turn a project into an image file: the image with `\-o`, the Z\-Map with `\-\-zmap`, either or both in one invocation. At least one of the two is required. This is the only command that writes an image
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the image to this path
.TP
\fB\-\-zmap\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the Z\-Map to this path
.TP
\fB\-\-checkpoint\fR \fI<ID>\fR
A checkpoint id or unique id prefix. Defaults to the head. An unedited image export needs no source frames; an edited one re\-reads and verifies the nearest fused ancestor\*(Aqs. `\-\-zmap` alone needs none
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
The image format to write: `tiff`, `png` or `jpeg`. Inferred from `\-o`\*(Aqs extension when omitted (`.tif`/`.tiff` \-> tiff, `.png` \-> png, `.jpg`/`.jpeg` \-> jpeg, no extension \-> tiff, the default); refused if it names a format other than a recognised extension\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-tiff\-bits\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
TIFF bit depth: `16` (default) or `8`. TIFF only
.TP
\fB\-\-tiff\-compression\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
TIFF strip compression: `none` (default), `lzw` or `deflate`. TIFF only
.TP
\fB\-\-png\-bits\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
PNG bit depth: `16` (default) or `8`. PNG only
.TP
\fB\-\-png\-compression\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
PNG compression effort: `fast`, `default` (default) or `best`. PNG only
.TP
\fB\-\-jpeg\-quality\fR \fI<N>\fR
JPEG quality, 1\-100, default 95. JPEG only
.TP
\fB\-\-jpeg\-subsampling\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
JPEG chroma subsampling: `420` (default) or `444`. JPEG only
.TP
\fB\-\-exif\fR \fI<EXIF>\fR
Carry the alignment reference frame\*(Aqs EXIF: `on` (default) or `off`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log detail (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-icc\fR \fI<ICC>\fR
Embed an ICC profile: `on` (default) or `off`
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Log errors only
.TP
\fB\-\-xmp\fR \fI<XMP>\fR
Carry the source frame\*(Aqs XMP packet verbatim: `on` or `off` (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-iptc\fR \fI<IPTC>\fR
Carry the source frame\*(Aqs IPTC block verbatim: `on` or `off` (default). Never written to PNG
.TP
\fB\-\-frame\fR \fI<INDEX>\fR
Write this source frame "as fused" \-\- warped by its recorded transform and offset by the applied crop, at the resolved checkpoint\*(Aqs own composite width and height. Requires `\-\-frame\-output`
.TP
\fB\-\-frame\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Where to write the frame `\-\-frame` names
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the JSON report instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The `.ffp` project to read
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0\-rc.4
